that removing the garnish makes it safe.","Offer it without mentioning the allergy."],"correct":1,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"Sesame oil appears in this dish’s allergen notes. Do not promise that an omission makes the dish safe; confirm the request with the manager and kitchen."},{"prompt":"How long does Yasai Meshi take to prepare?","options":["15 min","20 min","10 min","5 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The menu manual lists 10 minutes for Yasai Meshi. Check with the kitchen if a guest needs an updated timing estimate."}]},{"name":"Suika","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Fruity, spicy, with a balance between sweet and bitter notes.\n\nMeaning: Japanese name that means watermelon, the use of this product is due to its importance in Japan as a consumer.\n\nProcess: Put the ingredients in the glass with big ice, garnish kinome.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Japan has the famous square watermelons, they can be sold at a cost of 250 dollars and up, they are usually used as special gifts since they are not edible.\n\nElaboration Time: 1 minute\n\nClassification: Fresh - Aperitive\n\nNotes: Fruity, spicy, subtle bitter and sweet\n\nMethod: Building\n\nGlassware: Lima Glass\n\nObservations: No straw\n\nManual section: PISUKO TAIKEN - PISCO EXPERIENCE\nKERO BAR by Osaka is a brand that continues to expand globally and this section accompanies a distillate of Peruvian origin, seeking to show the versatility for cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 2.","ingredients":["Caravedo Acholado pisco","Cocchi americano","watermelon & mint cordial","lemon."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Suika?","options":["Roku gin","Toki whisky","Caravedo Acholado pisco","Haku vodka"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Suika recipe includes Caravedo Acholado pisco."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Suika?","options":["Haku vodka","watermelon & mint cordial","Toki whisky","Roku gin"],"correct":1,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Suika recipe includes watermelon & mint cordial."},{"prompt":"How is Suika mixed?","options":["Built in the glass","Shaken","Stirred","Blended"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Suika as Building."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Suika?","options":["Lima Glass","Bamboo glass","Rock glass","Coupe"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Suika in Lima Glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Suika take to prepare?","options":["1 min","2 min","5 min","3 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 1 minutes for Suika. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Suika. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team."],"correct":3,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Aka Sour","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"House pisco sour with citrus, sweet and spicy by cardamom, the notes evolve when mixed with ice made with chicha & wine.\n\nMeaning: Aka Japanese word meaning red. In conclusion, a red sour.\n\nProcess: Dry shake 10 seconds, shake with ice 14 seconds and serve on the botija.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): An evolutionary cocktail is one that does not maintain the same profile and shows new characteristics as time passes.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minute\n\nClassification: Sour - Aperitive\n\nNotes: Semi dry, citrus, spicy, evolutionary\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Lima Glass & Botija\n\nObservations: No straw - served on the table\n\nManual section: PISUKO TAIKEN - PISCO EXPERIENCE\nKERO BAR by Osaka is a brand that continues to expand globally and this section accompanies a distillate of Peruvian origin, seeking to show the versatility for cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 3.","ingredients":["Caravedo Quebranta pisco","lime","cardamom syrup","egg white. Chicha morada ice."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Aka Sour?","options":["Roku gin","Toki whisky","Caravedo Quebranta pisco","Haku vodka"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Aka Sour recipe includes Caravedo Quebranta pisco."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Aka Sour?","options":["Haku vodka","Roku gin","cardamom syrup","Toki whisky"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Aka Sour recipe includes cardamom syrup."},{"prompt":"How is Aka Sour mixed?","options":["Stirred","Shaken","Built in the glass","Blended"],"correct":1,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Aka Sour as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Aka Sour?","options":["Lima Glass & Botija","Coupe","Rock glass","Bamboo glass"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Aka Sour in Lima Glass & Botija, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Aka Sour take to prepare?","options":["3 min","5 min","1 min","2 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Aka Sour. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Aka Sour. What should you do?","options":["Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank."],"correct":2,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Sakura","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Refreshing cocktail with floral, fruity and citrus notes.\n\nMeaning: Cherry Blossom. The lotus base accompanies the beauty and illuminated color of the Sakura.\n\nProcess: Put the ingredients in the mixing glass, stir and serve. Put the cocktail on the Lotus base with the light on.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Cherry blossoms are the symbolic flower of spring, the time of renewal and the fleeting nature of life. It is through the cocktail that we seek to immortalize the Sakura.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Floral, fruity, citrus, fresh\n\nMethod: Stir\n\nGlassware: Lima glass and lotus base\n\nManual section: PISUKO TAIKEN - PISCO EXPERIENCE\nKERO BAR by Osaka is a brand that continues to expand globally and this section accompanies a distillate of Peruvian origin, seeking to show the versatility for cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 3.","ingredients":["Caravedo Torontel pisco","elixir rose","lychee liqueur","grapefruit","lime."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Sakura?","options":["Caravedo Torontel pisco","Roku gin","Haku vodka","Toki whisky"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Sakura recipe includes Caravedo Torontel pisco."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Sakura?","options":["Toki whisky","Haku vodka","Roku gin","lychee liqueur"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Sakura recipe includes lychee liqueur."},{"prompt":"How is Sakura mixed?","options":["Blended","Built in the glass","Stirred","Shaken"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Sakura as Stir."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Sakura?","options":["Bamboo glass","Coupe","Lima glass and lotus base","Rock glass"],"correct":2,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Sakura in Lima glass and lotus base, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Sakura take to prepare?","options":["5 min","1 min","3 min","2 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Sakura. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Sakura. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed."],"correct":2,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Ronin Chilcano","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Citrus, bubbly, light sweet and spiced by ginger. try wakamomo adding tropical notes.\n\nMeaning: The ronin was also known for his spirit of independence and rebellion. So this drink symbolizes rebellion and independence since it is not common to add liqueur to Chilcanos.\n\nProcess: Put the ingredients in the Collins glass and mix gently. Garnish the stick with wakamomo.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): The word ronin derives from the Japanese words ro meaning \"aimless\" and nin meaning \"person.\"\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, bubbly, light sweet, spiced\n\nMethod: Building\n\nGlassware: Long Drink\n\nManual section: PISUKO TAIKEN - PISCO EXPERIENCE\nKERO BAR by Osaka is a brand that continues to expand globally and this section accompanies a distillate of Peruvian origin, seeking to show the versatility for cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 4.","ingredients":["Caravedo Quebranta pisco infused in purple corn","yellow Chartreuse","yuzu","ginger ale","wakamomo."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Ronin Chilcano?","options":["Caravedo Quebranta pisco infused in purple corn","Haku vodka","Roku gin","Toki whisky"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Ronin Chilcano recipe includes Caravedo Quebranta pisco infused in purple corn."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Ronin Chilcano?","options":["yuzu","Roku gin","Toki whisky","Haku vodka"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Ronin Chilcano recipe includes yuzu."},{"prompt":"How is Ronin Chilcano mixed?","options":["Blended","Built in the glass","Stirred","Shaken"],"correct":1,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Ronin Chilcano as Building."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Ronin Chilcano?","options":["Lima Glass","Rock glass","Long Drink","Coupe"],"correct":2,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Ronin Chilcano in Long Drink, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Ronin Chilcano take to prepare?","options":["1 min","3 min","2 min","5 min"],"correct":1,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Ronin Chilcano. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Ronin Chilcano. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed."],"correct":1,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Pisco Sour","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Peruvian classic with citrus, subtle sweet and creamy notes.\n\nMeaning: Pisco is a word from Quechua, which means little bird or bird, as well as the name of a port in Ica.\n\nProcess: Dry shake 10 seconds, shake with ice 14 seconds and serve in the glass. Add drops of bitters.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Pisco sour was created on april 1, 1916 by Victor Morris. Mario Bruiget evolved Víctor Morris 's original recipe until arriving at the current formula.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, subtle sweet and creamy\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Coupe\n\nManual section: PISUKO TAIKEN - PISCO EXPERIENCE\nKERO BAR by Osaka is a brand that continues to expand globally and this section accompanies a distillate of Peruvian origin, seeking to show the versatility for cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 4.","ingredients":["Pisco","lime","simple syrup","egg white. Angostura bitters."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Pisco Sour?","options":["Pisco","Haku vodka","Toki whisky","Roku gin"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Pisco Sour recipe includes Pisco."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Pisco Sour?","options":["simple syrup","Roku gin","Haku vodka","Toki whisky"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Pisco Sour recipe includes simple syrup."},{"prompt":"How is Pisco Sour mixed?","options":["Stirred","Built in the glass","Shaken","Blended"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Pisco Sour as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Pisco Sour?","options":["Rock glass","Coupe","Lima Glass","Bamboo glass"],"correct":1,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Pisco Sour in Coupe, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Pisco Sour take to prepare?","options":["3 min","5 min","2 min","1 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Pisco Sour. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Pisco Sour. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank."],"correct":2,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Chilcano De Pisco","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Peruvian classic with citrus notes, light sweet and bubbly.\n\nMeaning: Pisco is a word from Quechua, which means little bird or bird, as well as the name of a port in Ica.\n\nProcess: Dry shake 10 seconds, shake with ice 14 seconds and serve in the glass. Add drops of bitters.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): It is said that at the end of the 19th century the Chilcano was created as a local variant of the popular American cocktail \"gin fizz\". European immigrants who arrived in Peru at that time, particularly Italian immigrants, introduced the use of ginger ale as a refreshing ingredient in cocktails.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, bubbly, light sweet, spiced\n\nMethod: Building\n\nGlassware: Long Drink\n\nManual section: PISUKO TAIKEN - PISCO EXPERIENCE\nKERO BAR by Osaka is a brand that continues to expand globally and this section accompanies a distillate of Peruvian origin, seeking to show the versatility for cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 5.","ingredients":["Pisco","lime","ginger ale","Angostura bitters."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Chilcano De Pisco?","options":["Roku gin","Haku vodka","Pisco","Toki whisky"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Chilcano De Pisco recipe includes Pisco."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Chilcano De Pisco?","options":["Haku vodka","Roku gin","ginger ale","Toki whisky"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Chilcano De Pisco recipe includes ginger ale."},{"prompt":"Which bitters go into Chilcano De Pisco?","options":["Toki whisky","Haku vodka","Roku gin","Angostura bitters"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Chilcano De Pisco recipe includes Angostura bitters."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Chilcano De Pisco?","options":["Lima Glass","Coupe","Long Drink","Rock glass"],"correct":2,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Chilcano De Pisco in Long Drink, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Chilcano De Pisco take to prepare?","options":["1 min","5 min","3 min","2 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Chilcano De Pisco. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Chilcano De Pisco. What should you do?","options":["Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team."],"correct":3,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Mr Osaka","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Cocktail with smoky, fresh, fruity notes.\n\nMeaning: It symbolizes Osaka because of the different characters, fresh because of the fruit, intense and serious because of the smoky notes, sparkling because of the bubbles.\n\nProcess: In a shaker add all the ingredients, shake and serve in a glass previously smoked with rosemary. Complete with tonic water. We decorate with orange zest rolled in rosemary.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Cocktail presented at the World Class Perú 2014, an international bar competition.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing - Smoke\n\nNotes: Fruity, spicy, subtle citrus, subtle smokiness\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Volcano ceramic\n\nObservations: Straw\n\nManual section: SEKAI KAKUTERU - KERO GLOBAL\nThis section reflects the cocktails that travel around the different Osakas globally. What you try here you can try there...\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 6.","ingredients":["Zacapa 23 & Flor de Caña 7 rum","lulo","basil syrup","Indian tonic","rosemary smoke."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Mr Osaka?","options":["Roku gin","Pisco","Haku vodka","Zacapa 23 & Flor de Caña 7 rum"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Mr Osaka recipe includes Zacapa 23 & Flor de Caña 7 rum."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Mr Osaka?","options":["Haku vodka","basil syrup","Roku gin","Pisco"],"correct":1,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Mr Osaka recipe includes basil syrup."},{"prompt":"How is Mr Osaka mixed?","options":["Stirred","Blended","Built in the glass","Shaken"],"correct":3,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Mr Osaka as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Mr Osaka?","options":["Lima Glass","Coupe","Volcano ceramic","Rock glass"],"correct":2,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Mr Osaka in Volcano ceramic, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Mr Osaka take to prepare?","options":["3 min","1 min","5 min","2 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Mr Osaka. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Mr Osaka. What should you do?","options":["Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients."],"correct":1,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Amai Shio","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Versatile cocktail, from citrus, sweet, spicy notes to a saline touch, with smoky expressions, generating balance of flavors.\n\nMeaning: Amai = Sweet / Shio = Salty in Japanese.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients except the togarashi, shake lightly and present in an old fashioned glass with togarashi rim and big ice.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Made by Viviana Cabiedes at a time when the heyday of mezcal was beginning, seeking the balance between sweet and salty.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Fruity, spicy, sweet, citrus, subtle smokiness\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Rock glass\n\nManual section: SEKAI KAKUTERU - KERO GLOBAL\nThis section reflects the cocktails that travel around the different Osakas globally. What you try here you can try there...\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 6.","ingredients":["Vida Mezcal","Toki whisky","spicy tincture","tangerine & rosemary cordial","passion fruit","salt","togarashi."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Amai Shio?","options":["Haku vodka","Vida Mezcal","Pisco","Roku gin"],"correct":1,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Amai Shio recipe includes Vida Mezcal."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Amai Shio?","options":["spicy tincture","Haku vodka","Pisco","Roku gin"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Amai Shio recipe includes spicy tincture."},{"prompt":"How is Amai Shio mixed?","options":["Built in the glass","Stirred","Shaken","Blended"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Amai Shio as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Amai Shio?","options":["Coupe","Lima Glass","Rock glass","Bamboo glass"],"correct":2,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Amai Shio in Rock glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Amai Shio take to prepare?","options":["2 min","3 min","5 min","1 min"],"correct":1,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Amai Shio. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Amai Shio. What should you do?","options":["Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients."],"correct":1,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Negroni Kunsei","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Cocktail inspired by the classic negroni with the personal touch of Osaka, with smoke notes, followed by an addition of citrus to tangerine with cocoa.\n\nMeaning: Smoked Negroni.\n\nProcess: Put the ingredients in the mixing glass, stir for 20 seconds and serve on the glass with an ice ball. Put the glass inside the box and smoke, close and open on the table.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Classic Negroni (1919 – 1920) composed of gin, Campari and vermouth by Fosco Scarselli for Camillo Negroni who used to drink the American cocktail.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Aperitif – Smoked\n\nNotes: Sweet, bitter, spiced\n\nMethod: Stir\n\nGlassware: Rock glass and wood box with light\n\nObservations: People remove the glass and the server takes the box\n\nManual section: SEKAI KAKUTERU - KERO GLOBAL\nThis section reflects the cocktails that travel around the different Osakas globally. What you try here you can try there...\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 7.","ingredients":["Roku gin","chocolate liqueur","Campari","Satsuma vermouth."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Negroni Kunsei?","options":["Roku gin","Toki whisky","Pisco","Haku vodka"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Negroni Kunsei recipe includes Roku gin."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Negroni Kunsei?","options":["Haku vodka","Campari","Pisco","Toki whisky"],"correct":1,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Negroni Kunsei recipe includes Campari."},{"prompt":"How is Negroni Kunsei mixed?","options":["Shaken","Blended","Stirred","Built in the glass"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Negroni Kunsei as Stir."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Negroni Kunsei?","options":["Rock glass and wood box with light","Coupe","Lima Glass","Bamboo glass"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Negroni Kunsei in Rock glass and wood box with light, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Negroni Kunsei take to prepare?","options":["3 min","1 min","5 min","2 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Negroni Kunsei. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Negroni Kunsei. What should you do?","options":["Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients."],"correct":1,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Sacred Tani","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"A citrus and refreshing cocktail, with marked herbal notes, where we use a liquor of Peruvian origin where botanicals from the Cusco area are used.\n\nMeaning: Sacred Valley, the sacred valley of the Incas is a valley in the Andes of Perú, in Cusco.\n\nProcess: Put the ingredients in the shaker, shake for 15 seconds and serve on the glass. In the stone base put dry ice and banana leaf, then put the glass with the cocktail.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Matacuy is the spirit of the Andes made with high Andean sugar cane, fresh herbs, fruits and spices. Sacred Tani is inspired by the last word cocktail, it is thought to date from immediately prior to Prohibition but owes its present-day popularity to being reincarnated in 2004 by Murray Stenson during his tenure at Seattle’s Zig Zag Café.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Aperitif and refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, herbal, slight sweetness\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Rock Glass and Stone base\n\nManual section: SEKAI KAKUTERU - KERO GLOBAL\nThis section reflects the cocktails that travel around the different Osakas globally. What you try here you can try there...\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 7.","ingredients":["Matacuy","Luxardo Maraschino","rice shochu","lime","pink peppercorn syrup."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Sacred Tani?","options":["Matacuy","Haku vodka","Roku gin","Pisco"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Sacred Tani recipe includes Matacuy."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Sacred Tani?","options":["Pisco","Haku vodka","rice shochu","Roku gin"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Sacred Tani recipe includes rice shochu."},{"prompt":"How is Sacred Tani mixed?","options":["Blended","Stirred","Built in the glass","Shaken"],"correct":3,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Sacred Tani as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Sacred Tani?","options":["Lima Glass","Rock Glass and Stone base","Coupe","Bamboo glass"],"correct":1,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Sacred Tani in Rock Glass and Stone base, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Sacred Tani take to prepare?","options":["1 min","2 min","3 min","5 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Sacred Tani. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Sacred Tani. What should you do?","options":["Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank."],"correct":2,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Honey Cha","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Sweet, citrus cocktail, where the liquid is mixed at the table with a matcha granite.\n\nMeaning: Tea with honey. This cocktail honors the tea ritual: Chanoyu.\n\nProcess: Mix the ingredients in a shaker and shake for 10 seconds, accompanied by the cup with the granita. The experience is completed by serving at the table.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): The ice game is important to show that it not only cools but can also add flavor. The Japanese phrase Chanoyu, translated literally as “hot water for tea,” refers to the tradition of preparing and serving powdered green tea in a highly stylized manner.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, sweet, subtle herbal\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Tea Set up ceramic\n\nManual section: SEKAI KAKUTERU - KERO GLOBAL\nThis section reflects the cocktails that travel around the different Osakas globally. What you try here you can try there...\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 8.","ingredients":["Rice shochu","Zubrowka vodka","yuzu","honey","sencha granite."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Honey Cha?","options":["Rice shochu","Haku vodka","Roku gin","Pisco"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Honey Cha recipe includes Rice shochu."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Honey Cha?","options":["yuzu","Pisco","Haku vodka","Roku gin"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Honey Cha recipe includes yuzu."},{"prompt":"How is Honey Cha mixed?","options":["Blended","Stirred","Built in the glass","Shaken"],"correct":3,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Honey Cha as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Honey Cha?","options":["Lima Glass","Rock glass","Tea Set up ceramic","Coupe"],"correct":2,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Honey Cha in Tea Set up ceramic, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Honey Cha take to prepare?","options":["3 min","1 min","5 min","2 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Honey Cha. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Honey Cha. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team."],"correct":3,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Shiso Bata","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Oily texture from the fatwash, with notes of nuts, sweet, spice and a subtle herbaceousness from the shiso.\n\nMeaning: Shiso is a leaf that comes from the perilla plant. Bata is a Japanese word that means butter, we use this for fat wash.\n\nProcess: In a mixing glass, gently press the shiso, then add the ingredients and stir. Add Shiso in the glass, then ice ball and serve cocktail.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): There are two types of shiso, green (ojiso) and purple (akajiso). We use ojiso. Old fashioned, Over many decades this vintage classic has changed name (it was originally the Whisky Cocktail) and has evolved with both the methods deployed to make it and its ingredients by bartending fashions.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Aperitive\n\nNotes: Spiced, sweet, subtle herbal\n\nMethod: Stir\n\nGlassware: Rock glass\n\nManual section: NEITIBU - NATIVE\nHere we seek to give value to each location so that they can express their creativity as well as make known unique products transmitted in the cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 8.","ingredients":["Sagamore rye fatwash","junmai sake","chocolate liqueur","shiso leaf","black walnut bitters","salt."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Shiso Bata?","options":["Roku gin","Pisco","Sagamore rye fatwash","Haku vodka"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Shiso Bata recipe includes Sagamore rye fatwash."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Shiso Bata?","options":["Haku vodka","Roku gin","Pisco","chocolate liqueur"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Shiso Bata recipe includes chocolate liqueur."},{"prompt":"How is Shiso Bata mixed?","options":["Built in the glass","Blended","Stirred","Shaken"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Shiso Bata as Stir."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Shiso Bata?","options":["Bamboo glass","Lima Glass","Rock glass","Coupe"],"correct":2,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Shiso Bata in Rock glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Shiso Bata take to prepare?","options":["3 min","2 min","1 min","5 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Shiso Bata. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Shiso Bata. What should you do?","options":["Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed."],"correct":0,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Midori Snake","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Very expressive of tropical, sweet and fruity notes with botanical notes that complete the cocktail.\n\nMeaning: Midori is green in Japanese, given by melon liquor. The snake is because of the glassware, when it was developed it was sought to capture the skin of the anaconda on the walls.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients and shake. Serve on the ceramic with crushed ice.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): London Dry Gins are different from other styles of gin because they contain no extra sugar or additives. Midori® melon liqueur was inspired by a Japanese visionary. Shinjiro Torii, founder of suntory.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Fruity, sweet, citrus\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Snake ceramic\n\nObservations: Straw\n\nManual section: NEITIBU - NATIVE\nHere we seek to give value to each location so that they can express their creativity as well as make known unique products transmitted in the cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 9.","ingredients":["N°3 gin","Matacuy","Midori","pineapple","kiwi jam","lime."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Midori Snake?","options":["Roku gin","Pisco","N°3 gin","Haku vodka"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Midori Snake recipe includes N°3 gin."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Midori Snake?","options":["Midori","Pisco","Haku vodka","Roku gin"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Midori Snake recipe includes Midori."},{"prompt":"How is Midori Snake mixed?","options":["Blended","Stirred","Built in the glass","Shaken"],"correct":3,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Midori Snake as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Midori Snake?","options":["Lima Glass","Snake ceramic","Coupe","Rock glass"],"correct":1,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Midori Snake in Snake ceramic, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Midori Snake take to prepare?","options":["3 min","1 min","2 min","5 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Midori Snake. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Midori Snake. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team."],"correct":3,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Tropical Shinigami","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Herbaceous and tropical notes, sweet and spicy, light citrus.\n\nMeaning: Shinigami in Japan is the god of death, we relate this to Mexican culture in relation to Catrina, symbol of death and that in November they celebrate such a day. We make a combination between life due to the tropical nature of the ingredients and the art of still life.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients, shake. Serve in the tin glass, complete with crushed ice. Decorate with flowers and dried bamboo.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Shrub , the original recipe of the Turks and Persians was more complex than the one that became popular, centuries later, in Europe. For them, the mixture included sugar, citrus fruit juice, flowers, herbs, and even nuts. The second adaptation moved away from the traditional recipe, the mixture of vinegar and sugar, two natural preservatives.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Fruity, subtle spicy, sweet, citrus\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Tin Glass\n\nObservations: Straw\n\nManual section: NEITIBU - NATIVE\nHere we seek to give value to each location so that they can express their creativity as well as make known unique products transmitted in the cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 9.","ingredients":["Tequila blanco infused in shishito pepper","grapefruit liqueur","grapefruit","guava shrub","mirin."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Tropical Shinigami?","options":["Roku gin","Haku vodka","Pisco","Tequila blanco infused in shishito pepper"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Tropical Shinigami recipe includes Tequila blanco infused in shishito pepper."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Tropical Shinigami?","options":["grapefruit","Roku gin","Pisco","Haku vodka"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Tropical Shinigami recipe includes grapefruit."},{"prompt":"How is Tropical Shinigami mixed?","options":["Blended","Built in the glass","Shaken","Stirred"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Tropical Shinigami as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Tropical Shinigami?","options":["Coupe","Lima Glass","Rock glass","Tin Glass"],"correct":3,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Tropical Shinigami in Tin Glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Tropical Shinigami take to prepare?","options":["2 min","3 min","5 min","1 min"],"correct":1,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Tropical Shinigami. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Tropical Shinigami. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank."],"correct":2,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Kero Diamante","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"We seek to care for the Macallan notes, with notes of citrus fruits and spices, with an oily texture that allows complexity in the flavor.\n\nMeaning: Kero Diamante refers to elegance and luxury in the drink.\n\nProcess: The mixture is ready in the flask, accompanied by a glass with diamond ice on a masu with dry ice.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): This special single malt is inspired by the ethiopian arabica bean. Ethiopia is claimed to be the birthplace of coffee as the arabica bean was the first species of coffee to be cultivated. This special single malt exudes flavors of sweet oak, tiramisu and dark chocolate.\n\nElaboration Time: 2 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Fruity, spiced, lightly sweet\n\nMethod: Building\n\nGlassware: Asian flask / Kings rock / Masu\n\nManual section: NEITIBU - NATIVE\nHere we seek to give value to each location so that they can express their creativity as well as make known unique products transmitted in the cocktails.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 10.","ingredients":["The Macallan Harmony & 12","lucuma","kumquat","plum","oolong tea","white chocolate","mirin."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Kero Diamante?","options":["Pisco","The Macallan Harmony & 12","Roku gin","Haku vodka"],"correct":1,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Kero Diamante recipe includes The Macallan Harmony & 12."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Kero Diamante?","options":["kumquat","Pisco","Roku gin","Haku vodka"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Kero Diamante recipe includes kumquat."},{"prompt":"How is Kero Diamante mixed?","options":["Stirred","Shaken","Blended","Built in the glass"],"correct":3,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Kero Diamante as Building."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Kero Diamante?","options":["Lima Glass","Asian flask / Kings rock / Masu","Coupe","Rock glass"],"correct":1,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Kero Diamante in Asian flask / Kings rock / Masu, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Kero Diamante take to prepare?","options":["3 min","1 min","2 min","5 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 2 minutes for Kero Diamante. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Kero Diamante. What should you do?","options":["Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank."],"correct":2,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Hokkaido Mule","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Inspired by the Moscow Mule (john martin & jack morgan – 1941), with citrus and spicy notes.\n\nMeaning: Hokkaido is home to one of the world's leading breweries, which is why we dedicated the name to the cocktail inspired by the Moscow Mule.\n\nProcess: Put the ingredients in the cup and mix gently. Complete with ice crush and ginger dust.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): The Moscow Mule was invented somewhere around 1941, and more than one person is suspected to be the inventor. John G. Martin claims that he and Jack Morgan, the owner of the Los Angeles British pub Cock ‘n’ Bull were the first ones to create the drink. However, that story doesn’t have to be true.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, sweet, spicy\n\nMethod: Building\n\nGlassware: Copper mug\n\nManual section: KOTEN KERO - CLASSIC KERO STYLE\nWe honor classic cocktails, adding the Nikkei touch.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 11.","ingredients":["Haku vodka","yuzu","lemongrass syrup","ginger beer","ginger dust."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Hokkaido Mule?","options":["Roku gin","Toki whisky","Haku vodka","Pisco"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Hokkaido Mule recipe includes Haku vodka."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Hokkaido Mule?","options":["lemongrass syrup","Pisco","Toki whisky","Roku gin"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Hokkaido Mule recipe includes lemongrass syrup."},{"prompt":"How is Hokkaido Mule mixed?","options":["Shaken","Built in the glass","Blended","Stirred"],"correct":1,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Hokkaido Mule as Building."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Hokkaido Mule?","options":["Copper mug","Lima Glass","Rock glass","Coupe"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Hokkaido Mule in Copper mug, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Hokkaido Mule take to prepare?","options":["1 min","2 min","3 min","5 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Hokkaido Mule. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Hokkaido Mule. What should you do?","options":["Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team."],"correct":3,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Hai - Ball","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Subtle bubbly, like fruit and light citrus.\n\nMeaning: Inspired by the highball cocktail, Hai is a Japanese word that refers to confirmation and acceptance, which we will confirm with the enjoyment of the guest.\n\nProcess: Build the cocktail in the longdrink with collins ice.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Thought of the modern classic highball (patrick duffy – 1894), whisky and soda.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Lightly sweet and spiced, subtle citrus\n\nMethod: Building\n\nGlassware: Long drink Riedel\n\nObservations: No straw\n\nManual section: KOTEN KERO - CLASSIC KERO STYLE\nWe honor classic cocktails, adding the Nikkei touch.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 11.","ingredients":["Hibiki Harmony whisky","umeshu","plum shrub","soda."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Hai - Ball?","options":["Roku gin","Pisco","Hibiki Harmony whisky","Haku vodka"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Hai - Ball recipe includes Hibiki Harmony whisky."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Hai - Ball?","options":["Roku gin","Haku vodka","plum shrub","Pisco"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Hai - Ball recipe includes plum shrub."},{"prompt":"How is Hai - Ball mixed?","options":["Blended","Built in the glass","Stirred","Shaken"],"correct":1,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Hai - Ball as Building."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Hai - Ball?","options":["Long drink Riedel","Lima Glass","Rock glass","Coupe"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Hai - Ball in Long drink Riedel, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Hai - Ball take to prepare?","options":["2 min","5 min","1 min","3 min"],"correct":3,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Hai - Ball. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Hai - Ball. What should you do?","options":["Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team."],"correct":3,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Penishirin","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Inspired by the modern classic penicillin (sam ross - 2005), we play with wasabi and japanese whiskey for the mix. with citrus, sweet and spicy notes.\n\nMeaning: Japanese word that means penicillin.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients, shake. Serve in the glass, garnish caviar and black salt.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): The Penicillin cocktail was created by Sam Ross in the mid-2000s, when he was working at New York City’s famous Milk & Honey bar.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Sweet, spiced, citrus, subtle smoke\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Rock glass\n\nManual section: KOTEN KERO - CLASSIC KERO STYLE\nWe honor classic cocktails, adding the Nikkei touch.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 12.","ingredients":["Toki whisky","Laphroaig whisky","ginger syrup","lemongrass","honey."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Penishirin?","options":["Toki whisky","Pisco","Roku gin","Haku vodka"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Penishirin recipe includes Toki whisky."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Penishirin?","options":["Roku gin","Pisco","Haku vodka","ginger syrup"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Penishirin recipe includes ginger syrup."},{"prompt":"How is Penishirin mixed?","options":["Shaken","Blended","Stirred","Built in the glass"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Penishirin as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Penishirin?","options":["Rock glass","Lima Glass","Bamboo glass","Coupe"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Penishirin in Rock glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Penishirin take to prepare?","options":["2 min","1 min","3 min","5 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Penishirin. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Penishirin. What should you do?","options":["Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients."],"correct":0,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Esupuresso Kokotini","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Inspired by espresso martini (dick bradsell - 1983), with sweet and light toast notes with tropical coconut miso, some cremosity.\n\nMeaning: Esupuresso is a Japanese word that means espresso, kokotini is a play on words between coconut and martini.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients, shake. Serve in the coupe glass, garnish golden coffee.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Dick Bradsell . He is credited with revolutionizing the cocktail scene in London in the 1980s, originally called The Vodka Espresso then the Pharmaceutical Stimulant – at Fred’s Club\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Digestive\n\nNotes: Lightly bitter, creamy, tropical\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Coupe glass\n\nManual section: KOTEN KERO - CLASSIC KERO STYLE\nWe honor classic cocktails, adding the Nikkei touch.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 12.","ingredients":["Haku vodka","coconut liqueur","coffee","coconut miso syrup."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Esupuresso Kokotini?","options":["Roku gin","Toki whisky","Pisco","Haku vodka"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Esupuresso Kokotini recipe includes Haku vodka."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Esupuresso Kokotini?","options":["Pisco","coffee","Toki whisky","Roku gin"],"correct":1,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Esupuresso Kokotini recipe includes coffee."},{"prompt":"How is Esupuresso Kokotini mixed?","options":["Stirred","Built in the glass","Blended","Shaken"],"correct":3,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Esupuresso Kokotini as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Esupuresso Kokotini?","options":["Rock glass","Bamboo glass","Coupe glass","Lima Glass"],"correct":2,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Esupuresso Kokotini in Coupe glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Esupuresso Kokotini take to prepare?","options":["3 min","2 min","5 min","1 min"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Esupuresso Kokotini. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Esupuresso Kokotini. What should you do?","options":["Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed."],"correct":0,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Coco Bang","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Fresh with tropical, floral and light citrus notes.\n\nMeaning: Coco is a Spanish word that means coconut. Coconut with an explosion of flavors, shots of sensations that will generate reactions in the brain.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients, shake. Serve in the black ceramic, garnish kumquat paper and baby breaths flower.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Genmaicha is the mixture of toasted brown rice with green tea.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Tropical fruit, floral, lightly citrus\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Black ceramic\n\nObservations: Straw\n\nManual section: ARUKORU NASHI - SIN ALCOHOL\nInteresting part, because it is the search to provide an alcohol-free experience that makes the senses vibrate.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 13.","ingredients":["Coconut miso syrup","genmaicha kumquat cordial","lulo","orange blossom."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Coco Bang?","options":["Coconut miso syrup","Roku gin","Haku vodka","Pisco"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Coco Bang recipe includes Coconut miso syrup."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Coco Bang?","options":["Pisco","Roku gin","lulo","Haku vodka"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Coco Bang recipe includes lulo."},{"prompt":"How is Coco Bang mixed?","options":["Stirred","Built in the glass","Shaken","Blended"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Coco Bang as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Coco Bang?","options":["Black ceramic","Coupe","Rock glass","Lima Glass"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Coco Bang in Black ceramic, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Coco Bang take to prepare?","options":["2 min","1 min","3 min","5 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Coco Bang. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Coco Bang. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank."],"correct":1,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Yuzu Tea","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Citrus, sweet fruity and creamy.\n\nMeaning: Yuzu the citrus part and tea the herbal note, this cocktail plays with the textures of both the liquid and the foam.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients, shake. Serve in the glass and complete with yuzu foam.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): ”Sencha” means cooked tea, the invention of Nagatani Soen in 1738.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, sweet, herbal, creamy\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Bamboo glass\n\nManual section: ARUKORU NASHI - SIN ALCOHOL\nInteresting part, because it is the search to provide an alcohol-free experience that makes the senses vibrate.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 13.","ingredients":["Sencha infusion","pineapple yuzu cordial","yuzu foam."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Yuzu Tea?","options":["Pisco","Haku vodka","Roku gin","Sencha infusion"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Yuzu Tea recipe includes Sencha infusion."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Yuzu Tea?","options":["Pisco","Roku gin","Haku vodka","yuzu foam"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Yuzu Tea recipe includes yuzu foam."},{"prompt":"How is Yuzu Tea mixed?","options":["Built in the glass","Stirred","Shaken","Blended"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Yuzu Tea as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Yuzu Tea?","options":["Coupe","Bamboo glass","Lima Glass","Rock glass"],"correct":1,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Yuzu Tea in Bamboo glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Yuzu Tea take to prepare?","options":["1 min","5 min","3 min","2 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Yuzu Tea. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Yuzu Tea. What should you do?","options":["Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team."],"correct":3,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Chicha Morada","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Peruvian classic with a spiced touch from pink pepper.\n\nMeaning: Peruvian classic with a touch of the house.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients, shake. Serve in bamboo glass. Garnish dried pineapple.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Although currently the preparation of Chicha morada does not go through a fermentation process, in the past, the Incas fermented it for a short time to achieve a greater flavor. With the arrival of the Spanish, this technique fell into disuse and, instead, ingredients such as pineapple, cloves, cinnamon, apple and lemon juice were included.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, sweet, spiced, fruity\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Bamboo glass\n\nManual section: ARUKORU NASHI - SIN ALCOHOL\nInteresting part, because it is the search to provide an alcohol-free experience that makes the senses vibrate.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 14.","ingredients":["Purple corn infusion","pineapple","apple","spices","lime","pink peppercorn syrup."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Chicha Morada?","options":["Roku gin","Pisco","Haku vodka","Purple corn infusion"],"correct":3,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Chicha Morada recipe includes Purple corn infusion."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Chicha Morada?","options":["Haku vodka","Pisco","apple","Roku gin"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Chicha Morada recipe includes apple."},{"prompt":"How is Chicha Morada mixed?","options":["Built in the glass","Stirred","Shaken","Blended"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Chicha Morada as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Chicha Morada?","options":["Bamboo glass","Coupe","Lima Glass","Rock glass"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Chicha Morada in Bamboo glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Chicha Morada take to prepare?","options":["1 min","2 min","3 min","5 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Chicha Morada. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Chicha Morada. What should you do?","options":["Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team."],"correct":3,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"OSK Fresh","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Light bubbly, subtle spicy, fruity sweet, citrus.\n\nMeaning: Looking for a refreshing option without alcohol, fruity, herbal and bubble notes were mixed that added sweetness to achieve a balanced drink ready to refresh the palate.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients, shake. Serve in oval glass and garnish fresno, bamboo leaf.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Deeply rooted in the “terroir” of vergèze in the south of France, perrier® relies on the quality of its natural mineral water to deliver its legendary taste.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Citrus, fruity sweet, subtle spice\n\nMethod: Building\n\nGlassware: Oval glass\n\nManual section: ARUKORU NASHI - SIN ALCOHOL\nInteresting part, because it is the search to provide an alcohol-free experience that makes the senses vibrate.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 14.","ingredients":["Tangerine cordial","rosemary","soda."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in OSK Fresh?","options":["Haku vodka","Tangerine cordial","Roku gin","Pisco"],"correct":1,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The OSK Fresh recipe includes Tangerine cordial."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into OSK Fresh?","options":["Pisco","soda","Haku vodka","Roku gin"],"correct":1,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The OSK Fresh recipe includes soda."},{"prompt":"Which herb is used in OSK Fresh?","options":["Haku vodka","Roku gin","Rosemary","Pisco"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The OSK Fresh recipe includes Rosemary."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for OSK Fresh?","options":["Rock glass","Oval glass","Lima Glass","Coupe"],"correct":1,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve OSK Fresh in Oval glass, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does OSK Fresh take to prepare?","options":["1 min","3 min","5 min","2 min"],"correct":1,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for OSK Fresh. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in OSK Fresh. What should you do?","options":["Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank.","Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients."],"correct":2,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]},{"name":"Blossom Lemonade","content_type":"cocktails","expected_source":{"description":"Make a refreshing drink with floral, citrus and floral notes, contributed by Sakura tea, watermelon and lime.\n\nProcess: In a shaker with ice, add all the ingredients, shake. Serve in the glass jar. Sakura candy leaf.\n\nExtra fact (from the manual): Sakura tea is a blend between cherry blossom and green tea.\n\nElaboration Time: 3 minutes\n\nClassification: Refreshing\n\nNotes: Fruity, floral, citrus\n\nMethod: Shake\n\nGlassware: Glass jar\n\nManual section: ARUKORU NASHI - SIN ALCOHOL\nInteresting part, because it is the search to provide an alcohol-free experience that makes the senses vibrate.\n\nSource: Osaka Cocktail Description Manual 2024, page 15.","ingredients":["Sakura tea infusion","watermelon mint cordial","lime."],"allergens":[]},"questions":[{"prompt":"Which ingredient is used in Blossom Lemonade?","options":["Haku vodka","Pisco","Sakura tea infusion","Roku gin"],"correct":2,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Blossom Lemonade recipe includes Sakura tea infusion."},{"prompt":"Which of these also goes into Blossom Lemonade?","options":["lime","Roku gin","Pisco","Haku vodka"],"correct":0,"topic":"Ingredients","explanation":"The Blossom Lemonade recipe includes lime."},{"prompt":"How is Blossom Lemonade mixed?","options":["Shaken","Built in the glass","Blended","Stirred"],"correct":0,"topic":"Preparation method","explanation":"The manual lists the method for Blossom Lemonade as Shake."},{"prompt":"Which glassware is used for Blossom Lemonade?","options":["Glass jar","Coupe","Rock glass","Lima Glass"],"correct":0,"topic":"Glassware","explanation":"Serve Blossom Lemonade in Glass jar, as specified in the cocktail manual."},{"prompt":"How long does Blossom Lemonade take to prepare?","options":["2 min","5 min","3 min","1 min"],"correct":2,"topic":"Preparation time","explanation":"The cocktail manual lists 3 minutes for Blossom Lemonade. Check current timing with the bar team when needed."},{"prompt":"A guest asks about allergies in Blossom Lemonade. What should you do?","options":["Check the full recipe and confirm with the manager and bar team.","Check only the main spirit and ignore the other ingredients.","Promise it is safe if the garnish is removed.","Say it has no allergens because the allergen field is blank."],"correct":0,"topic":"Guest allergy requests","explanation":"The cocktail allergen information has not been completed. A blank field does not mean allergen-free. Check every ingredient and preparation detail with the manager and bar team."}]}]$bank$::jsonb) as x(name text,content_type text,expected_source jsonb,questions jsonb);
create temporary table quiz_targets as select m.id,q.* from quiz_refresh q join public.menu_items m on m.name=q.name and m.content_type=q.content_type join public.restaurants r on r.id=m.restaurant_id join auth.users u on u.id=r.owner_id where r.name='Osaka - Miami' and u.email='castem93@gmail.com';
do $$ begin
if (select count(*) from quiz_targets)<>85 then raise exception 'Expected 85 uniquely matched items'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from quiz_targets q join public.menu_items m on m.id=q.id where q.expected_source is distinct from jsonb_build_object('description',m.description,'ingredients',m.ingredients,'allergens',m.allergens)) then raise exception 'Menu sources changed; review before publishing'; end if;
end $$;
insert into public.quiz_bank_revisions(menu_item_id,questions) select e.menu_item_id,e.questions from public.menu_quiz_edits e join quiz_targets q on q.id=e.menu_item_id where e.questions is distinct from q.questions;
insert into public.menu_quiz_edits(menu_item_id,questions) select id,questions from quiz_targets on conflict(menu_item_id) do update set questions=excluded.questions;
select count(*) as published_quizzes,sum(jsonb_array_length(e.questions)) as published_questions from public.menu_quiz_edits e join quiz_targets q on q.id=e.menu_item_id;
commit;
